From d843fb17e031b3cc9903db67f431016030d6e91a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:58:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] [AArch64] Support the musl ILP32 environment
 (musl_ilp32)

Add the environment musl_ilp32 for the AArch64 ILP32 ABI with musl, as in
aarch64-openwrt-linux-musl_ilp32 (OpenWrt's aarch64 ILP32 toolchain). It uses
the same data model and calling convention as gnu_ilp32.

- Triple::MuslILP32, parsed before "musl"; isMusl() includes it, and the
  new Triple::isILP32Environment() is true for gnu_ilp32 and musl_ilp32.
- Use isILP32Environment() where only GNUILP32 was checked: the data layout,
  the ELF EH encoding, the AArch64 backend (isTargetILP32, isTargetGNUILP32),
  the MC layer and clang's data model.
- Driver: -mabi=ilp32 and -mabi=lp64 switch between musl and musl_ilp32 as
  they do between gnu and gnu_ilp32; the dynamic linker is
  /lib/ld-musl-aarch64[_be]_ilp32.so.1 and the ld emulation
  aarch64linux32[b]. The libilp32 directory, the multiarch triple and the
  glibc dynamic linker stay GNU-only: musl ILP32 keeps its libraries in lib.

Signed-off-by: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
